            "is_markdown": true,
            "bug_id": 19164,
            "text": "Created attachment 3841\noptionally include `xreg` in `arima()` output\n\nHere is a patch proposal to optionally include `xreg` in `arima()` output, as suggested in https://stat.ethz.ch/pipermail/r-devel/2026-September/084691.html.\n\nNotes:\n\n- Usage of capitalization and terminal punctuation is not uniform in the `\\arguments{}` section; happy to \"fix\" that if preferred.\n- Perhaps it may be useful to also update the description to make the role of `xreg` explicit, e.g.:\n\n```\n-  Fit an ARIMA model to a univariate time series.\n+  Fit an ARIMA model, or a linear regression with ARMA errors when external regressors are provided, to a univariate time series.\n```",
            "creation_time": "2026-09-08T22:27:14Z",
            "creator": "Thomas.SOEIRO"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
